    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221-a4">

                <pb facs="0534" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg438"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 262.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">J. Lambert, esq., to
                        Mr. Litchfield.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Calcutta</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 20,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1767.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your letter No. 252, of
                    the 13th instant, regarding a murde committed on the high seas on board the
                    American bark C. O. Whitmore, I have the <pb facs="0535" n="439" xml:id="pg439"
                    /> honor to imform you that I have, through the solicitor to the government,
                    obtained the opinion of the advocate-general, who states that the accused, John
                    Anderson, should be tried by the high court of Calcutta in its admiralty
                    jurisdiction. The case will therefore be placed before the presidency magistrate
                    of the southern division this day at 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. LAMBERT,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy Commissioner of
                            Police.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
